{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.8c211cc02e","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-c-395","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Juniper National Park is in southern Norway. It was established in 1995.</li><li>Its area is 2,697 square kilometers.</li><li>Halden National Park is in southern New Zealand. It was established in 1951.</li><li>Its area is 1,211 square kilometers.</li><li>Both are parks known for their old-growth forests.</li></ul><p>The student wants to emphasize how the area of the two parks differs.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Juniper National Park, which is in southern Norway, is one of several parks known for their old-growth forests.","The area of Juniper National Park (2,697 square kilometers) is greater than that of Halden National Park (1,211 square kilometers).","Juniper National Park was established in 1995, while Halden National Park was established in 1951.","Both Juniper National Park and Halden National Park are parks known for their old-growth forests."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It compares the area of both parks. The other choices describe a similarity, a difference in date, or only one park."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.313ce40ba9","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-c-397","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>The Umber Museum is in central Spain. It opened in 1929.</li><li>Its annual attendance is 319,340 visitors.</li><li>The Halden Museum is in eastern Australia. It opened in 1918.</li><li>Its annual attendance is 309,707 visitors.</li><li>Both are museums of natural history.</li></ul><p>The student wants to emphasize how the annual attendance of the two museums differs.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The Umber Museum, which is in central Spain, is one of several museums of natural history.","The Umber Museum opened in 1929, while the Halden Museum opened in 1918.","Both the Umber Museum and the Halden Museum are museums of natural history.","The annual attendance of the Umber Museum (319,340 visitors) is greater than that of the Halden Museum (309,707 visitors)."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It compares the annual attendance of both museums. The other choices describe a similarity, a difference in date, or only one museum."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.213816ed89","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-7","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Priya Mensah is an ecologist.</li><li>Mensah wanted to find out whether city lights change when songbirds begin singing in the morning.</li><li>Mensah compared the first songs of robins in brightly lit city parks with those in dark rural woodlands.</li><li>Mensah found that robins in lit parks began singing nearly an hour earlier.</li><li>Mensah concluded that artificial light may shift birds' daily rhythms.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Mensah found that robins in lit parks began singing nearly an hour earlier.","Mensah concluded that artificial light may shift birds' daily rhythms.","Ecologist Priya Mensah set out to learn whether city lights change when songbirds begin singing in the morning.","To investigate the question, Mensah compared the first songs of robins in brightly lit city parks with those in dark rural woodlands."],"answer":"A","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.2d8e148de1","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-25","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Elias Takeda is a materials scientist.</li><li>Takeda wanted to find out whether a coating made from seaweed can keep fruit fresh longer.</li><li>Takeda coated half of a batch of strawberries with a seaweed-based film and left the rest uncoated.</li><li>Takeda found that coated strawberries stayed fresh for about four days longer.</li><li>Takeda concluded that the coating could help reduce food waste.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Takeda concluded that the coating could help reduce food waste.","To investigate the question, Takeda coated half of a batch of strawberries with a seaweed-based film and left the rest uncoated.","Materials scientist Elias Takeda set out to learn whether a coating made from seaweed can keep fruit fresh longer.","Takeda found that coated strawberries stayed fresh for about four days longer."],"answer":"D","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.dc2988bf38","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-27","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Ravi Moreau is a materials scientist.</li><li>Moreau wanted to find out whether a coating made from seaweed can keep fruit fresh longer.</li><li>Moreau coated half of a batch of strawberries with a seaweed-based film and left the rest uncoated.</li><li>Moreau found that coated strawberries stayed fresh for about four days longer.</li><li>Moreau concluded that the coating could help reduce food waste.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Moreau coated half of a batch of strawberries with a seaweed-based film and left the rest uncoated.","Materials scientist Ravi Moreau set out to learn whether a coating made from seaweed can keep fruit fresh longer.","Moreau found that coated strawberries stayed fresh for about four days longer.","Moreau concluded that the coating could help reduce food waste."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.5f60ffd9b8","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-29","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Tomás Varga is a materials scientist.</li><li>Varga wanted to find out whether a coating made from seaweed can keep fruit fresh longer.</li><li>Varga coated half of a batch of strawberries with a seaweed-based film and left the rest uncoated.</li><li>Varga found that coated strawberries stayed fresh for about four days longer.</li><li>Varga concluded that the coating could help reduce food waste.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Varga concluded that the coating could help reduce food waste.","Varga found that coated strawberries stayed fresh for about four days longer.","Materials scientist Tomás Varga set out to learn whether a coating made from seaweed can keep fruit fresh longer.","To investigate the question, Varga coated half of a batch of strawberries with a seaweed-based film and left the rest uncoated."],"answer":"D","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.2616d08c4e","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-36","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Leila Asante is a sociologist.</li><li>Asante wanted to find out whether community gardens increase how often neighbors talk to one another.</li><li>Asante surveyed residents before and one year after gardens opened in their neighborhoods.</li><li>Asante found that residents reported speaking with neighbors more often after the gardens opened.</li><li>Asante concluded that community gardens may strengthen neighborhood ties.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Asante concluded that community gardens may strengthen neighborhood ties.","To investigate the question, Asante surveyed residents before and one year after gardens opened in their neighborhoods.","Asante found that residents reported speaking with neighbors more often after the gardens opened.","Sociologist Leila Asante set out to learn whether community gardens increase how often neighbors talk to one another."],"answer":"B","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.b965b4d450","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-38","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Sofia Solberg is a sociologist.</li><li>Solberg wanted to find out whether community gardens increase how often neighbors talk to one another.</li><li>Solberg surveyed residents before and one year after gardens opened in their neighborhoods.</li><li>Solberg found that residents reported speaking with neighbors more often after the gardens opened.</li><li>Solberg concluded that community gardens may strengthen neighborhood ties.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Solberg concluded that community gardens may strengthen neighborhood ties.","Solberg found that residents reported speaking with neighbors more often after the gardens opened.","Sociologist Sofia Solberg set out to learn whether community gardens increase how often neighbors talk to one another.","To investigate the question, Solberg surveyed residents before and one year after gardens opened in their neighborhoods."],"answer":"D","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.9da217e731","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-61","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Viktor Varga is an astronomer.</li><li>Varga wanted to find out whether a distant star's brightness changes on a regular schedule.</li><li>Varga measured the star's brightness every night for eighteen months.</li><li>Varga found that the star dimmed slightly about every 42 days.</li><li>Varga concluded that an orbiting planet may be passing in front of the star.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Astronomer Viktor Varga set out to learn whether a distant star's brightness changes on a regular schedule.","Varga concluded that an orbiting planet may be passing in front of the star.","To investigate the question, Varga measured the star's brightness every night for eighteen months.","Varga found that the star dimmed slightly about every 42 days."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.0c69ffd82e","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-64","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Imani Lindqvist is an astronomer.</li><li>Lindqvist wanted to find out whether a distant star's brightness changes on a regular schedule.</li><li>Lindqvist measured the star's brightness every night for eighteen months.</li><li>Lindqvist found that the star dimmed slightly about every 42 days.</li><li>Lindqvist concluded that an orbiting planet may be passing in front of the star.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Lindqvist concluded that an orbiting planet may be passing in front of the star.","Lindqvist found that the star dimmed slightly about every 42 days.","Astronomer Imani Lindqvist set out to learn whether a distant star's brightness changes on a regular schedule.","To investigate the question, Lindqvist measured the star's brightness every night for eighteen months."],"answer":"B","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.e6dea54caa","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-66","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Tomás Abara is a linguist.</li><li>Abara wanted to find out whether bilingual children are better at switching between tasks.</li><li>Abara gave bilingual and monolingual children a game that required switching rules quickly.</li><li>Abara found that bilingual children switched rules with fewer errors.</li><li>Abara concluded that speaking two languages may strengthen certain mental skills.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Abara concluded that speaking two languages may strengthen certain mental skills.","Abara found that bilingual children switched rules with fewer errors.","Linguist Tomás Abara set out to learn whether bilingual children are better at switching between tasks.","To investigate the question, Abara gave bilingual and monolingual children a game that required switching rules quickly."],"answer":"B","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.b7993f90be","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-78","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Ayumi Abara is a botanist.</li><li>Abara wanted to find out whether tomato plants grow better with music played nearby.</li><li>Abara grew tomato plants in two identical greenhouses, one with music and one without.</li><li>Abara found that plants in both greenhouses grew at similar rates.</li><li>Abara concluded that music may have little effect on tomato growth.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Botanist Ayumi Abara set out to learn whether tomato plants grow better with music played nearby.","To investigate the question, Abara grew tomato plants in two identical greenhouses, one with music and one without.","Abara found that plants in both greenhouses grew at similar rates.","Abara concluded that music may have little effect on tomato growth."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.3fa78785f0","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-92","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Ingrid Castellano is a hydrologist.</li><li>Castellano wanted to find out whether wetlands reduce flooding downstream.</li><li>Castellano compared river levels below restored wetlands with levels below drained farmland after storms.</li><li>Castellano found that river levels rose more slowly below the wetlands.</li><li>Castellano concluded that wetlands may help protect nearby communities from floods.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Hydrologist Ingrid Castellano set out to learn whether wetlands reduce flooding downstream.","To investigate the question, Castellano compared river levels below restored wetlands with levels below drained farmland after storms.","Castellano found that river levels rose more slowly below the wetlands.","Castellano concluded that wetlands may help protect nearby communities from floods."],"answer":"B","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.d1ce637742","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-94","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Samuel Halvorsen is a hydrologist.</li><li>Halvorsen wanted to find out whether wetlands reduce flooding downstream.</li><li>Halvorsen compared river levels below restored wetlands with levels below drained farmland after storms.</li><li>Halvorsen found that river levels rose more slowly below the wetlands.</li><li>Halvorsen concluded that wetlands may help protect nearby communities from floods.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Halvorsen found that river levels rose more slowly below the wetlands.","Hydrologist Samuel Halvorsen set out to learn whether wetlands reduce flooding downstream.","Halvorsen concluded that wetlands may help protect nearby communities from floods.","To investigate the question, Halvorsen compared river levels below restored wetlands with levels below drained farmland after storms."],"answer":"D","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.74a04fbc93","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-96","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Hana Brennan is an education researcher.</li><li>Brennan wanted to find out whether reading aloud to young children improves their vocabulary.</li><li>Brennan had parents in one group read aloud daily while another group continued their usual routines.</li><li>Brennan found that children in the read-aloud group learned more new words.</li><li>Brennan concluded that regular read-aloud time may support vocabulary growth.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Brennan had parents in one group read aloud daily while another group continued their usual routines.","Education researcher Hana Brennan set out to learn whether reading aloud to young children improves their vocabulary.","Brennan found that children in the read-aloud group learned more new words.","Brennan concluded that regular read-aloud time may support vocabulary growth."],"answer":"A","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.76daf38186","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-105","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Amara Kowalski is a chemist.</li><li>Kowalski wanted to find out whether a new plant-based plastic breaks down in seawater.</li><li>Kowalski placed samples of the plastic in tanks of seawater for six months.</li><li>Kowalski found that most samples broke apart within four months.</li><li>Kowalski concluded that the plastic may be less harmful to oceans than conventional plastic.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Kowalski placed samples of the plastic in tanks of seawater for six months.","Chemist Amara Kowalski set out to learn whether a new plant-based plastic breaks down in seawater.","Kowalski found that most samples broke apart within four months.","Kowalski concluded that the plastic may be less harmful to oceans than conventional plastic."],"answer":"A","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.936dce9c56","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-108","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Leila Varga is a primatologist.</li><li>Varga wanted to find out whether young chimpanzees learn to use tools by watching adults.</li><li>Varga observed young chimpanzees in groups where adults cracked nuts with stones and in groups where adults did not.</li><li>Varga found that young chimpanzees in the nut-cracking groups began using stones much earlier.</li><li>Varga concluded that young chimpanzees may learn tool use by observation.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Varga found that young chimpanzees in the nut-cracking groups began using stones much earlier.","Primatologist Leila Varga set out to learn whether young chimpanzees learn to use tools by watching adults.","To investigate the question, Varga observed young chimpanzees in groups where adults cracked nuts with stones and in groups where adults did not.","Varga concluded that young chimpanzees may learn tool use by observation."],"answer":"A","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.a28b7fcddb","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-125","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Felipe Okafor is an ornithologist.</li><li>Okafor wanted to find out whether birds that migrate farther have longer wings.</li><li>Okafor measured the wings of several related species with different migration distances.</li><li>Okafor found that species that migrated farther tended to have longer, narrower wings.</li><li>Okafor concluded that wing shape may be linked to migration distance.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Okafor measured the wings of several related species with different migration distances.","Ornithologist Felipe Okafor set out to learn whether birds that migrate farther have longer wings.","Okafor found that species that migrated farther tended to have longer, narrower wings.","Okafor concluded that wing shape may be linked to migration distance."],"answer":"A","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.214be14b86","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-129","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Felipe Novak is a public health researcher.</li><li>Novak wanted to find out whether adding bike lanes increases how often residents cycle.</li><li>Novak counted cyclists on streets before and after new bike lanes were added.</li><li>Novak found that cycling on those streets nearly doubled within a year.</li><li>Novak concluded that bike lanes may encourage more people to ride.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Novak counted cyclists on streets before and after new bike lanes were added.","Novak concluded that bike lanes may encourage more people to ride.","Public health researcher Felipe Novak set out to learn whether adding bike lanes increases how often residents cycle.","Novak found that cycling on those streets nearly doubled within a year."],"answer":"D","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.b00b1e92e1","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-143","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Tomás Castellano is a neuroscientist.</li><li>Castellano wanted to find out whether learning to juggle changes brain structure.</li><li>Castellano scanned volunteers' brains before and after three months of juggling practice.</li><li>Castellano found that regions linked to tracking movement grew slightly larger.</li><li>Castellano concluded that practicing a new skill may reshape parts of the brain.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Castellano concluded that practicing a new skill may reshape parts of the brain.","Castellano found that regions linked to tracking movement grew slightly larger.","Neuroscientist Tomás Castellano set out to learn whether learning to juggle changes brain structure.","To investigate the question, Castellano scanned volunteers' brains before and after three months of juggling practice."],"answer":"D","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.1df0ffc79e","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-151","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Chen Duarte is a climate scientist.</li><li>Duarte wanted to find out whether light-colored roofs reduce indoor temperatures.</li><li>Duarte compared indoor temperatures in homes with white roofs and homes with dark roofs.</li><li>Duarte found that homes with white roofs stayed several degrees cooler.</li><li>Duarte concluded that light-colored roofs may reduce the need for air-conditioning.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Duarte compared indoor temperatures in homes with white roofs and homes with dark roofs.","Climate scientist Chen Duarte set out to learn whether light-colored roofs reduce indoor temperatures.","Duarte found that homes with white roofs stayed several degrees cooler.","Duarte concluded that light-colored roofs may reduce the need for air-conditioning."],"answer":"A","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.1e4718eeeb","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-157","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Yara Mbeki is a behavioral economist.</li><li>Mbeki wanted to find out whether shoppers buy more fruit when it is placed near the store entrance.</li><li>Mbeki moved the fruit display to the entrance in some stores but not others.</li><li>Mbeki found that fruit sales rose in the stores with entrance displays.</li><li>Mbeki concluded that product placement may influence shoppers' choices.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Mbeki found that fruit sales rose in the stores with entrance displays.","Behavioral economist Yara Mbeki set out to learn whether shoppers buy more fruit when it is placed near the store entrance.","To investigate the question, Mbeki moved the fruit display to the entrance in some stores but not others.","Mbeki concluded that product placement may influence shoppers' choices."],"answer":"A","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.81c4d799e3","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-160","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Jonas Asante is a behavioral economist.</li><li>Asante wanted to find out whether shoppers buy more fruit when it is placed near the store entrance.</li><li>Asante moved the fruit display to the entrance in some stores but not others.</li><li>Asante found that fruit sales rose in the stores with entrance displays.</li><li>Asante concluded that product placement may influence shoppers' choices.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Asante found that fruit sales rose in the stores with entrance displays.","Behavioral economist Jonas Asante set out to learn whether shoppers buy more fruit when it is placed near the store entrance.","To investigate the question, Asante moved the fruit display to the entrance in some stores but not others.","Asante concluded that product placement may influence shoppers' choices."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.7b26a156d1","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-161","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Jonas Solberg is a behavioral economist.</li><li>Solberg wanted to find out whether shoppers buy more fruit when it is placed near the store entrance.</li><li>Solberg moved the fruit display to the entrance in some stores but not others.</li><li>Solberg found that fruit sales rose in the stores with entrance displays.</li><li>Solberg concluded that product placement may influence shoppers' choices.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Solberg concluded that product placement may influence shoppers' choices.","Behavioral economist Jonas Solberg set out to learn whether shoppers buy more fruit when it is placed near the store entrance.","Solberg found that fruit sales rose in the stores with entrance displays.","To investigate the question, Solberg moved the fruit display to the entrance in some stores but not others."],"answer":"D","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.3c4e197d20","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-168","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Viktor Kowalski is a forest ecologist.</li><li>Kowalski wanted to find out whether fungi help trees share nutrients.</li><li>Kowalski added a traceable form of carbon to some trees and checked nearby trees for it.</li><li>Kowalski found that the carbon appeared in neighboring trees connected by fungal networks.</li><li>Kowalski concluded that fungal networks may move nutrients between trees.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Kowalski added a traceable form of carbon to some trees and checked nearby trees for it.","Kowalski concluded that fungal networks may move nutrients between trees.","Kowalski found that the carbon appeared in neighboring trees connected by fungal networks.","Forest ecologist Viktor Kowalski set out to learn whether fungi help trees share nutrients."],"answer":"A","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.2ad2403e72","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-171","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Priya Varga is a forest ecologist.</li><li>Varga wanted to find out whether fungi help trees share nutrients.</li><li>Varga added a traceable form of carbon to some trees and checked nearby trees for it.</li><li>Varga found that the carbon appeared in neighboring trees connected by fungal networks.</li><li>Varga concluded that fungal networks may move nutrients between trees.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Varga added a traceable form of carbon to some trees and checked nearby trees for it.","Varga concluded that fungal networks may move nutrients between trees.","Forest ecologist Priya Varga set out to learn whether fungi help trees share nutrients.","Varga found that the carbon appeared in neighboring trees connected by fungal networks."],"answer":"D","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."}
